	"summary": {
		"text": "The Igbo are one of Nigeria’s three largest peoples, native to Abia, Anambra, Ebonyi, Enugu and Imo. Igbo is the lingua franca of the South East. Igboid peoples west of the Niger and in Rivers (Anioma, Ika, Ukwuani, Etche, Ogba, Ikwerre) are mapped under their own names, because many of them reject the Igbo label, though others among them, and Igbo organisations, count them as Igbo.",
